 "result": "Start with these:\n\n- **`src/tessel/app.py:1453`** – `run_app_teardowns(self, ctx, exc)`. It iterates `on_app_teardown_funcs` in reverse and passes `exc` to each.\n- **`src/tessel/ctx.py:496`** – the caller, `self.app.run_app_teardowns(self, exc)`. The surrounding `pop()` code (around line 273 and up) is where `exc` gets its value. It is typically `None` unless an unhandled exception is being propagated, in which case it is that exception.\n- **`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:828`** – the `on_app_teardown` registration and its docstring.\n\nFor observed behaviour, see `tests/test_appctx.py` (around lines 47–230), which exercises teardowns with and without errors. `docs/appcontext.rst:157` and `docs/lifecycle.rst:155` describe the intended semantics.",
